    "episode_evidence": "In this episode, Jack Mallers emphasizes the significance of Bitcoin's properties as a monetary unit, stating, 'Bitcoin's going to go up more than other assets because of the properties that it has as a monetary unit because it is scarcer because it is easier to store because it is easier to move because it is more private.' He also discusses the geopolitical tensions, particularly focusing on the impact of the U.S. Navy's actions on global supply chains, as he mentions, 'global supply chains are going to fall apart.' Mallers highlights the economic implications, noting that 'the world is loaded up on dollars and dollar-based assets. If they need to raise cash... they're going to have to sell dollars and dollar-based assets.' These points underscore the argument that Bitcoin could serve as a hedge against economic instability and outperform other assets in the face of geopolitical tensions and potential economic disruptions.",
